dinner and i went with bulldog noodles  these are like a ramen instant ramen i'm  also cooking some rice cakes in here as  well i love this because it's so yummy  but also so quick to make and for a  hungry girl like me i need it now three  i'm gonna eat and go to bed a lot of  people ask me how to handle these  situations from an intuitive eating  perspective when you know you sometimes  have to eat at more unusual meal times  when you're not really hungry so again  it's important to remember that  intuitive eating is not the hunger  fullness diet so if you eat when you're  not hungry or you don't stop when you're  full you're not doing this wrong this is  about self-care treat yourself and  sometimes if you know that you're  walking into a meeting or event where  you can't so easily eat and you maybe  aren't hungry now but you know that you  will be them it's best to preemptively  have a meal or snack to keep yourself  comfortable this is an act of self-care  treat yourself it's okay if your normal  meal has to be split into two meals or  you need a bedtime snack afterwards when  maybe you normally don't it's the  intuitive thing to do to think ahead to  prevent this hangry meltdown i know  personally i would have been like toast  by midnight and completely incapable of  cooking a meal so i would have like  front loaded a big meal pre event and  had a small easy snack before bed but  remy is younger than me so she can  probably rally a lot better than me she  has a bad hangover which she is  pretending as allergies so while i'm not  sure what kind of event she was at and  why she couldn't have access to any food  at the event if this is what worked for  her it works for me now if i had any  meal balancing tips it would just be to  maybe like add an extra egg and maybe  some nutritional yeast to bump up the  protein to promote better blood sugar  control as you sleep finally let's talk  dessert so remy doesn't have dessert  every night but she does mention that  she craves chocolate and junk food when  she's on her period so one night she has  some bits of a chocolate bar and another  night she has a bowl of ice cream both  delicious choices in my books and food  cravings during our cycle are actually  scientifically proven so research  suggests that there may be a  relationship between leptin and estrogen  hormones and the food cravings that we  experience when leptin levels are low  and estrogen levels are higher we may be  more likely to desire carb rich sweet  foods all of this is totally normal and  in my opinion not something that we need  to suppress but knowing that remy has  pcos which often has implications for  blood sugar management and that we tend  to see lower insulin sensitivity in the  evening i would try to dress up those  naked carbs to turn them into more  hunger crushing combos so maybe it's as  simple as just serving them with some  nuts on the side or on top so to sum us  up i applaud remy for taking a financial  challenge to try to cook more often at  home it looks like since our last  check-in remy has kind of relaxed a lot  of the diet rules in her day and we're  seeing more flexibility in her meals her  calorie intake also looks a lot more  substantial than we last checked in and  we're seeing a more equal spread of  macros as well my suggestion for someone  like remy as somebody also who has pcos  is to aim to amp up that breakfast meal  with some additional protein and carbs  to really take advantage of the  increased insulin sensitivity at that  time of day i would also try to dress up  those naked carbs with a little bit more  protein and fat to help stabilize the  blood sugar response and offer more  staying power as well i've watched a lot  of remy's content and while i know that  she does some kind of like mukbang  content and it often features more  stereotypical high calorie foods like  donuts i don't see her engaging in like  chaotic  over-the-top cheat day-like eating it  seems like a fun activity to do with  like-minded foodie friends to try out a  bunch of fun foods rather than a classic  cheat day food tour where she's eating  all of the donuts in one go so keep at  it remy and if you ever want to chat  about pcos and food you know who to call  and on that note that's all that i have  for you guys today if you like this  video be sure to give it the thumbs up  and thank you again to storington hall  for sponsoring remember you can install  the game using my link in the  description and get a bonus for new  players infinite lives for six hours  leave me a comment below on who or what  you'd like to see your view next  subscribe to the channel and i'll see  you next time on abby's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

